# zovwm keys.conf — reference / example.
#
# The real file lives at ~/.config/zovwm/keys.conf and is created
# automatically the first time zovwm runs (via the first-run wizard).
# This copy is annotated to read through or copy lines out of; dropping it
# in as-is works too (it's exactly the compiled-in defaults), but editing
# this file directly does nothing — only ~/.config/zovwm/keys.conf is read.
#
# Run `zovwm --list-keys` any time for the same action reference plus
# whatever's already in your own keys.conf, without opening this file.
#
# Format: one bind per line, blank lines and '#' comments ignored.
#
#   Mod+Mod+Key action [arg...]
#
# Modifiers: Super, Shift, Ctrl, Alt — combine with '+', e.g.
# "Super+Shift+j". Key is any name XStringToKeysym() accepts (X11 keysym
# names — letters/digits as themselves, plus names like "Return", "Left",
# "F1", "Tab", "space"...). Edits apply live: hit Super+Shift+r, or just
# save the file (zovwm watches ~/.config/zovwm/ and reloads automatically
# within about a second).

# --- window/focus management ---
Super+j            focus_next
Super+k            focus_prev
Super+Shift+j      move_next
Super+Shift+k      move_prev
Super+h            mfact_dec
Super+l            mfact_inc
Super+f            toggle_floating
Super+Shift+q      kill

# --- directional cursor/window movement ---
Super+Left         cursor_left
Super+Right        cursor_right
Super+Up           cursor_up
Super+Down         cursor_down
Super+Shift+Left   move_left
Super+Shift+Right  move_right
Super+Shift+Up     move_up
Super+Shift+Down   move_down

# --- layouts ---
Super+t            layout_fullscreen
Super+m            layout_monocle
Super+b            layout_bstack
Super+g            layout_grid

# --- workspaces: view/tag take a 1-9 workspace number as their argument.
#     Only 1 and 2 are spelled out here to save space — in the real
#     generated file all of Super+1..9 / Super+Shift+1..9 are present. ---
Super+1            view 1
Super+Shift+1      tag 1
Super+2            view 2
Super+Shift+2      tag 2

# --- launching apps: "spawn" takes the rest of the line as argv, split on
#     whitespace — no shell involved, so no quoting/pipes/env expansion. ---
Super+Return       spawn xterm
Super+p            spawn dmenu_run
Super+d            spawn rofi -show drun
Super+w            spawn zovwm-wallpaper

# --- wm control ---
Super+Shift+r      reload
Super+Shift+p      power_menu
Super+Shift+e      quit

# --- keyboard layout: cycles through whatever setxkbmap already
#     configured this session (e.g. "setxkbmap -layout us,ru" in
#     .xinitrc — see dotfiles/). No-op with only one layout active. ---
Super+space        kb_layout_next

# --- adding your own binds: pick any Mod+Mod+Key combo not already used
#     above, any action name from `zovwm --list-keys`, and (for
#     spawn/view/tag) an argument. A few examples — uncomment or adapt: ---
#
# Bind a file manager:
# Super+e              spawn thunar
#
# Give grid layout a second key, alongside Super+g:
# Super+Shift+g        layout_grid
#
# Screen lock via an external tool:
# Super+Ctrl+l         spawn slock
